  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Electronic Readmission Case Management System Implementation in T&#xFC;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the action is to contribute to the Government of T&#xFC;rkiye&#x2019;s efforts in ensuring the safe, dignified, and rights-based readmission of foreign nationals who are not eligible to stay in the country. The specific objective is to support T&#xFC;rkiye in streamlining and standardizing its readmission workflow to priority countries of origin,[1] ensuring data integrity, quality, and inter-operability. 
 
[1] PMM, at the time of developing this DoA, identified Algeria, Bangladesh, Morocco, Turkmenistan, and Uzbekistan as the priority countries of origin. However, in the project cycle, guided by Government of T&#xFC;rkiye&#x2019;s priorities, these countries may change subject to the progress made on readmission cooperation between T&#xFC;rkiye and these countries of origin.</narrative>
  </description>
